# Proposed Wiring

> **Status: PROPOSED wiring.** This is a recommended demonstration configuration. It is **not** a record of the original project's hardware, which has not been confirmed. Verify every connection against the datasheet of the exact modules you buy before applying power.

## 1. Pin-to-Pin Table (Arduino Uno, 5 V logic)

| # | From (component pin) | To (Arduino / node) | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Flame module VCC | 5V | Module runs from 5 V |
| 2 | Flame module GND | GND | Common ground |
| 3 | Flame module AO | A0 | Analog output used by code |
| 4 | Flame module DO | *not connected* | Digital output unused (threshold set in software) |
| 5 | MQ-2 module VCC | 5V | Heater draws about 150 mA |
| 6 | MQ-2 module GND | GND | Common ground |
| 7 | MQ-2 module AO | A1 | Analog output used by code |
| 8 | MQ-2 module DO | *not connected* | Unused |
| 9 | D4 | 220 Ω → Green LED anode | Cathode to GND |
| 10 | D5 | 220 Ω → Red LED anode | Cathode to GND |
| 11 | D6 | 220 Ω → Amber/blue LED anode | **Simulated suppression indicator**; cathode to GND |
| 12 | D7 | Push-button pin 1 | Pin 2 to GND (internal pull-up used) |
| 13 | D8 | 1 kΩ → NPN base (2N2222 / BC547) | Buzzer driver |
| 14 | NPN emitter | GND | |
| 15 | NPN collector | Buzzer negative (−) | |
| 16 | Buzzer positive (+) | 5V | Active buzzer, 5 V type |
| 17 | *(optional)* LCD I2C VCC / GND | 5V / GND | 16x2 I2C backpack |
| 18 | *(optional)* LCD I2C SDA / SCL | A4 / A5 | Set `USE_LCD 1`; address 0x27 or 0x3F |
| 19 | *(optional)* Servo signal | D9 | Set `USE_SERVO 1` |
| 20 | *(optional)* Servo V+ / GND | **External 5 V supply** | Share GND with Arduino |

## 2. Electrical Checks

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| LED current (5 V, 220 Ω, red ≈ 2 V) | ≈ 13.6 mA per LED. Under the 20 mA recommended per pin. |
| Total GPIO current | 3 LEDs ≈ 35–40 mA plus buzzer base ≈ 4 mA. Far below the ATmega328P 200 mA package limit. |
| Buzzer | Active 5 V buzzers can draw ~30 mA, above the 20 mA recommended per pin. The NPN transistor stage avoids loading the GPIO. |
| Transistor base current | (5 − 0.7) V / 1 kΩ ≈ 4.3 mA. Adequate to saturate for ≈ 30 mA load. |
| Flame module AO | Powered at 5 V, AO swings 0–5 V. Safe for the Uno's 5 V ADC. |
| MQ-2 module AO | Powered at 5 V, AO can reach ~5 V. Safe for Uno. |
| 3.3 V boards (ESP32, Pico, etc.) | **Do not connect 5 V analog outputs directly.** Power the module at 3.3 V (and re-calibrate) or use a resistor divider (e.g., 10 kΩ / 20 kΩ). Confirm the module's output behavior at 3.3 V first. |
| Power budget (USB) | Uno + MQ-2 heater + modules + LEDs is typically within USB 500 mA. Servo must **not** be powered from the Arduino 5 V pin. |
| Magnetic buzzers | If you use a magnetic (coil) buzzer, add a 1N4148 flyback diode across it (cathode to +). |

> Module pinouts and output polarity vary between manufacturers. Measure AO with a multimeter before connecting it to the Arduino.

