## 4. Optional: Relay Module (Low-Voltage Demonstration Load Only)

If you want to switch a real indicator load, you may connect an **opto-isolated relay module input** to D6 (instead of the amber LED) and set `SUPPRESSION_ACTIVE_HIGH` to match the module's logic (many modules are active-LOW).

Allowed for the educational demo: a low-voltage DC indicator lamp or small buzzer, within the relay's rating, powered from its own supply.

**Not allowed without proper engineering review:** mains-powered equipment, pumps, solenoid valves, pressurized systems, extinguishing agents, or any hazardous load. See the README Safety section.

## 5. Optional: Servo as Simulated Suppression Mechanism

- Power from a separate 5 V supply (1–2 A). A stalled micro-servo can draw several hundred mA.
- Connect supply GND to Arduino GND.
- Use the servo only to move a flag or lever as a visual demonstration. It must not release any fluid, gas, or powder.
- Note: the Servo library disables `analogWrite()` (PWM) on pins 9 and 10 on the Uno.
